407:| R-0511 | Representative design proofs before Core freezes, then cumulative slices with honest theorem scopes | the four A2b theorems are kernel-checked against the proposed `Spec.lean`, without `native_decide`, with their full obligations (decision row Q9.14): `reset_fresh` (a reset gives a brand distinct from every live brand, resets in a loop give pairwise-distinct brands, and the new allocator's operations refuse values of an old brand); `defer_cleanup_releases` (every structured exit runs the deferred calls in reverse registration order, releases each held loan after its call, and preserves the allocator-dependency check); `open_mut_freezes_root` (a mutable heap open excludes every other access to its root, and a shared open never grants a write); `rep_roundtrip` (encode then decode is the identity for `u8` to `u64`, `bool` and the empty struct); each later slice states its theorem scope (A2a was approved 2026-11-05) | — |
