461:| R-0593 | The diagnostic and facts records, their frozen, versioned JSON schema, goldens and the parser's diagnostics from the first front-end output ([diagnostics decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-project-diagnostics-2026-11-06), [early decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-07-early-evidence)) | every slice-0 refusal is one typed record rendered as human text and JSON lines (`--format=human|json`), with rule IDs from the Lean rule name and that rule's own revision (R-0603); the diagnostics and facts JSON schema is frozen and versioned from the first front-end output, and golden tests cover it and both diagnostic renderings; the LL(1) parser fills its expected-token set from the grammar data; B0's classified refusal controls use the records; Home: spec (the diagnostics and facts types are the schema source). Gate: the JSON schema generated from the Lean types, with goldens ([tracking](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-07-tracking)) | R-0592, R-0575 |
462:| R-0594 | Zero-heap facts proved in slice 0 ([decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-project-memory-2026-11-06)) | every slice-0 function's heap facts are 0, established by the derivation (no allocator is reachable), not by schema defaults; a planted reachable allocator flips them | R-0575, R-0592 |
463:| R-0585 | Vacuity checks and contract-strength labels from the first proof slice | no fact reads "proved" when its theorem holds only under an unsatisfiable precondition or premise set, from the first proof slice on; the checker reports a context as infeasible wherever its octagon is empty, and a discharge inside an infeasible context is marked vacuous, never established, unless the infeasibility itself is the claim (a dead branch), applying OD120 from B1 rather than F; each proved claim carries its strength (a point instance, one direction, an equivalence or a full contract), so a single-input proof never reads as a universal contract; planted vacuous and point-only proofs are caught; obligation sufficiency stays with R-0460 and the phase-F validation project with R-0219 | R-0575 |
