docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md:15:Before freezing, implement these contracts in the authoritative Lean library, with readable comments, accepted/refused examples and counterexamples to invalid premises. Discharge the four Q9.14 design theorems and the [A2i interaction/erasure obligations](../decisions.md#decided-project-long-term-2026-11-06), including the laws below. Tests alone do not establish them. Existing `ConcreteSpec` fragments are starting material, not evidence that omitted pointer fragments, external frames, initialization or cleanup interactions are already covered. Review and owner approval precede the freeze. This is a writing proposal, not that completed review or approval.
docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md:46:Layout laws: positive power-of-two alignment; size a multiple of aggregate alignment; occupied field bytes in bounds and non-overlapping; required field alignment in native/C modes; unique discriminants; and valid tag decoding. Only if question 5 adopts niches (unused encodings used for variants), require sound niche decoding and eligibility proofs. No niche machinery is required while niches are absent. Zero-size fields have empty byte ranges and may share offsets. Packed mode replaces natural field alignment with explicit unaligned-access premises; it must not falsely prove packed fields naturally aligned. Core uses the hybrid state in C4, with target/layout as a read-only parameter for sizeof/alignof and raw access. Safe typed operations are proved representation-independent where their premises permit it. The concrete algorithm below is one implementation proving these laws, not the premise of every earlier proof.
docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md:60:**State choice (question 2):** Core and its Lean evaluator use one hybrid state: structured places for safe typed storage, plus byte/provenance blocks for raw and exposed storage. A partial place-to-block/range projection and Rep relate the two. They are not independently writable copies. Safe borrow-view formation retains the structured root/projection and does not itself materialize bytes. Raw address-taking, expose, or passing an address to foreign code materializes the containing storage with a stable block/range mapping; existing materialized storage is reused. sizeof/alignof query layout without materializing storage. Materialization encodes active fields and pointer fragments and selects allowed initialization/byte contents for padding once through C8’s oracle.
docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md:111:**Freeze:** both the small-step relation and Q9.9's total fuel-indexed evaluator over instrumented hybrid Core state: `eval(target, layout, environmentChoices, fuel, coreProgram, state)`. This is the reference evaluator for qualification; it executes Core, not BIR or source text. Choices explicitly cover external responses, allocation/address choices, exposed-pointer alternatives and padding materialization. A choice input can be an oracle rather than a finite stream; each answer is checked against the operation contract. Oracle queries are pure deterministic functions of the Core execution history, request kind, logical site and occurrence number, independent of fuel budget; answers are deterministic functions of those queries and the fixed oracle. Materialization queries occur only at C4’s first raw exposure, not on safe borrowing or typed rewrites. Fixed inputs make evaluation deterministic. Native backends need not issue the same queries; P4 checks allowed Core observations instead. Prove evaluator soundness (a reported result has a matching finite execution), completeness (every finite execution is obtained with enough fuel), monotonicity (extra fuel preserves a completed result) and trace-prefix consistency. For nondeterministic effects these statements quantify over the same environment choices.
docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md:113:Prove infinite-behavior adequacy too: compatible limits of fuel-indexed execution prefixes correspond to infinite maximal executions, and every such execution has those prefixes. Carry states and steps as well as event traces: silent divergence has infinitely many steps but only finitely many events; infinite interaction has infinitely many events. An endlessly blocked run retains its blocking classification. Independent finite witnesses do not establish a compatible infinite run. This follows Q9.9 and [A1, “Fuel and divergence”](../../legacy/docs/compiler/A1_BOUNDARIES.md).
docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md:123:**Rule:** use independent typing, ownership, authority and execution judgments, with checker equivalence and elaborator correspondence. Keep safety evidence bound to typed identities, target, contracts and checker/spec versions. Recheck generic substitutions and Mono admission; compose checked summaries across calls/modules without reading bodies to guess effects. Struct-invariant rules remain those in the SPARK decision: private-field struct invariants hold at every exposure, with the spec definition written before freeze; the source feature waits for slice 17 (question 15). Contracts are erased logical assertions. Q9.11 and OD144 put ensures after all deferred cleanup, observing the result and only surviving parameter state. A consumed or scope-cleaned parameter is unavailable; body locals are never in function-contract scope. Entry values are read by requires, not implicitly saved for ensures. Q9.11’s authoritative row notes, [OD117](../decisions.md#od117) and [CON-3](../../legacy/docs/spec/contracts.md#CON-3) explicitly forbid `old` and snapshot constructs. Express relations to pre-state values of consumed parameters as Lean theorems over entry and normal-return states, without retaining a runtime owner or reviving cleaned storage. Safety admission needs closed evidence; assumptions cannot manufacture it.
docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md:145:**Frontend:** retract P1's parse/print criterion. Define byte/token/grammar acceptance independently of the lexer/parser implementation, and source binding, typing and source-to-Core correspondence independently of resolve/elaboration. Prove lexer/parser correspondence to the independent grammar, resolution's binding preservation and elaboration's preservation of meaning, sequencing, cleanup, identities and source sites. Prove checker equivalence to independent admission judgments. Parse/print tests can supplement these proofs but cannot replace them. This retains Core Q8.3/Q9.13 and the decided direct frontend proofs.
docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md:149:**Certificates and maximal behavior:** retain the [compiler-execution decision](../decisions.md#decided-project-long-term-2026-11-06): every authoritative compilation emits kernel-checked certificates binding the exact source bytes through independent judgments/validated edges to the exact emitted BIR, and binding the actual backend input to it. A digest establishes identity, not semantic correspondence. Native execution of proved Lean definitions is not itself proof; any gap retains explicit compiler/runtime/toolchain assumptions. After slice 0 use the decided per-edge certificates.
docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md:159:No revision is enacted here. Each question in section 5 has its own answer; an umbrella approval cannot choose these independently.
docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md:177:<a id="q1"></a>**Q1. Foundation scope.** Recommend approving the interface/law boundary of C1–C10, with freeze only after implementation, kernel proofs, interaction tests, independent review and owner acceptance. Runner-up: freeze smaller integrated scopes incrementally. Neither approves the other numbered questions.
docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md:180:<a id="q4"></a>**Q4. Enum layout.** Recommend retaining the existing profile’s i32 tags for now, deferring a compact u8/u16/u32 algorithm to the aggregate/layout slice and a separate owner answer. Runner-up: approve now the smallest tag fitting the variant count (u8 ≤256, u16 ≤65,536, u32 ≤2^32), declaration-order tags, aligned common payload and rounded aggregate size, rejecting larger counts. This changes OD126/FFI-7 independently of question 3.
