ROADMAP.md:468:| R-0576 | The predictable policy ([decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-project-predictable-policy), 2026-11-06) | an optional module or project policy, built on the per-function facts (R-0575), refuses at compile time any function in its scope that allocates, blocks or calls foreign code, and, when the policy demands it, any function without termination evidence or a stack bound; admission requires established evidence of no allocation, no blocking and no foreign calls, so an unknown or incomplete fact is refused; the policy explicitly states whether named trusted assumptions are acceptable (Q13); a violation names the function, the fact and its source; the query reports which policy covers each function; a planted violation and a planted unknown fact are both refused; the policy is declared in the project's `Concrete.toml` ([decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-project-concrete-toml)) as typed, versioned data, a module may tighten it but never relax it, and dependencies are checked against the consumer's policy transitively and fail-closed; Home: tooling (the optional `Concrete.toml` policy over the facts; the mandatory slice-0 stack-budget refusal is R-0575's). Gate: the policy's refusal controls ([tracking](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-07-tracking)) | R-0575 |
